    <string name="guide_title">Emergency Survival Guide</string>
    <string name="guide1_title">1. DROP, COVER, HOLD ON</string>
    <string name="guide1_desc">Drop to your hands and knees. Cover your head and neck with your arms. Hold on to sturdy furniture until the shaking stops.</string>
    <string name="guide2_title">2. STAY INDOORS</string>
    <string name="guide2_desc">Do not run outside during an earthquake. Most injuries occur when people try to rush out in panic.</string>
    <string name="guide3_title">3. STAY AWAY FROM GLASS</string>
    <string name="guide3_desc">Stay away from windows, glass, exterior doors and walls, and anything that could fall.</string>
    <string name="guide4_title">4. IF TRAPPED</string>
    <string name="guide4_desc">Do not light a match. Cover your mouth with clothing. Tap on pipes or walls to alert rescuers. Use a whistle if available.</string>
